================================================================================
astro4j / JSol'Ex
================================================================================

Portions of SolScan's spectral-line identification, exposure calculation, and SHG reconstruction
logic are translated and adapted from the astro4j project (JSol'Ex, JSol'Ex CLI, jsolex-core),
by Cedric Champeau ("melix") and contributors.
    https://github.com/melix/astro4j

Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. A copy of the License is available at:
    http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0

astro4j does not ship a NOTICE file of its own to propagate. Per-file attribution is instead
retained in the header of each SolScan source file that closely translates a specific astro4j
source file, pointing back to the original.

Specifically adapted, at time of writing (see CLAUDE.md for the full, current list; not yet
implemented, still on the roadmap):
  - DeepLineIdentifier (spectral line identification via reference-atlas correlation)
  - SpectralLineCatalog (interesting-lines.txt secondary-line lookup)
  - SpectrumBrowser (dispersion-aware reference-spectrum rendering)
  - ExposureCalculator (recommended exposure/fps from instrument optics and solar ephemeris)
  - SpectroHeliograph / Setup (equipment-profile data shapes)
  - SolexVideoProcessor's wider pipeline (geometry/ellipse-fitting correction, banding/jagging/
    distortion corrections, Advanced Images/Debug image kinds, ImageMath scripts) - its
    processSingleFrame reconstruction loop specifically has landed, see below

Specifically adapted, actually landed (each also carries its own per-file header comment pointing
back to the original Java source, per CLAUDE.md):
  - SpectralRay (predefined spectral line catalog - SolScan.Core.Processing.SpectralRay)
  - LineDetectionMode, RotationKind, AutocropMode, ContrastEnhancement, GeneratedImageKind (process
    parameter enums - SolScan.Core.Processing)
  - SpectrumParams, GeometryParams, RequestedImages, ProcessParams (process parameter records,
    trimmed to the fields SolScan currently uses - see each type's own doc comment for what's
    deliberately excluded - SolScan.Core.Processing)
  - AverageImageCreator.computeAverageImage (SolScan.Processing.Shg.FrameAverager - ported as a
    sequential two-pass version, see its own doc comment)
  - SpectrumFrameAnalyzer's curve-fitting pipeline - findLocalMinimum/findMinima/
    findDistortionPolynomial/findPolynomialAround/refineFit/depthWeightedCenter/sigmaClippedFit
    (SolScan.Processing.Shg.SpectralLineCurvatureDetector - disk left/right border detection not
    ported, see its own doc comment for why that's a real, supported fallback mode of the original
    algorithm, not an invented shortcut)
  - LinearRegression.secondOrderRegression, both overloads (math module -
    SolScan.Processing.Math.LinearRegression)
  - SolexVideoProcessor.processSingleFrame - the 5-tap Gaussian-weighted reconstruction loop
    (SolScan.Processing.Shg.DiskReconstructor)
  - DirectoryKind, and GeneratedImageKind's own per-constant directoryKind() mapping (which output
    subfolder each generated image kind belongs in - SolScan.Core.Processing.DirectoryKind /
    GeneratedImageKindExtensions.GetDirectoryKind, folder-naming convention confirmed against
    NamingStrategyAwareImageEmitter.java)

